00:29:12,070 --> 00:29:19,400
How we talk about the tech failure actually changes the human interaction around it, something to maybe mull over next time your screen goes blank.

656
00:29:20,110 --> 00:29:23,650
plunging into a topic that, well, it's become almost universal, hasn't it?

657
00:29:23,840 --> 00:29:24,440
Oh, absolutely.

658
00:29:24,460 --> 00:29:28,660
The glorious and sometimes, let's be honest, maddening world of video calls.

659
00:29:29,380 --> 00:29:35,950
You know that feeling you're all set to connect and bam, technology throws like a digital wrench in the works.

660
00:29:36,030 --> 00:29:36,490
Absolutely.

661
00:29:37,280 --> 00:29:41,340
Whether it's for work, catching up with friends, even, you know, remote classes.

662
00:29:42,120 --> 00:29:43,690
We've all hit those moments.

663
00:29:43,730 --> 00:29:44,030
Yeah.

664
00:29:44,210 --> 00:29:47,550
The picture freezes, the sound cuts out, or someone just

665
00:29:48,880 --> 00:29:50,360
vanishes into the ether.

