Sorry, I can't hear you at all.

690
00:31:17,050 --> 00:31:17,930
Pretty direct.

691
00:31:17,950 --> 00:31:18,930
No ambiguity there.

692
00:31:19,060 --> 00:31:19,400
Right.

693
00:31:19,700 --> 00:31:22,730
And what about that little microphone icon, the one with the line through it?

694
00:31:22,930 --> 00:31:25,190
That seems to be the culprit like 90 percent of the time.

695
00:31:25,270 --> 00:31:25,970
Oh, absolutely.

696
00:31:26,550 --> 00:31:28,090
That means someone is on mute.

697
00:31:29,190 --> 00:31:33,200
It's, you know, a setting they've activated or maybe the software did it automatically.

698
00:31:33,480 --> 00:31:40,330
OK. You'll often hear people say it says you're on mute or maybe I think your mic might be turned off.

699
00:31:40,310 --> 00:31:41,110
Turned off.

700
00:31:41,130 --> 00:31:42,550
So that's just another way to say muted.

701
00:31:42,750 --> 00:31:43,070
Yes.

702
00:31:43,230 --> 00:31:43,930
Effectively, yeah.

703
00:31:44,570 --> 00:31:47,890
And to fix it, you need to turn mute off.

